If some MME-units-per-day X are included by an opioid-dosage then the opioid-dosage defines a half-dosage-target that equals some target-MME-units-per-day Y and Y = X * 0.5.
If a patient has a continuous-opioid-use and the continuous-opioid-use has a duration and the duration includes more than 3 days and the duration includes less than 1 week and the patient has an opioid-dosage and the opioid-dosage defines a half-dosage-target and there is a clinician then the clinician may reduce the opioid-dosage to the half-dosage-target during 2 days for an opioid-withdrawal-symptom-amelioration during an opioid-discontinuation for the patient.
